{# Module: Mounts - External storage and persistent directories #}
{% if external_mounts and (external_mounts.ro or external_mounts.rw or external_mounts.persistent or external_mounts.user_ro or external_mounts.user_rw) or original_path_mounts %}

# External Storage

The following external folders are available in your workspace:

{% if external_mounts.ro %}
## Read-Only Mounts (`./external/ro/`)

These folders are mounted read-only. You can read files but **cannot create, modify, or delete** them.

{% for mount in external_mounts.ro %}
- `./external/ro/{{ mount.name }}/` {% if mount.description %}- {{ mount.description }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if external_mounts.rw %}
## Read-Write Mounts (`./external/rw/`)

These folders allow both reading and writing. Files you create or modify here will be visible to the host system.

{% for mount in external_mounts.rw %}
- `./external/rw/{{ mount.name }}/` {% if mount.description %}- {{ mount.description }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if external_mounts.persistent %}
## Persistent Storage (`./persistent/`)

This folder persists across sessions. Files you save here will be available in future sessions.

**IMPORTANT:** When the user asks to save something "permanently", "persistently", "across sessions", or "for later use", **always save to `./persistent/`**.

**Use for:**
- Files the user explicitly wants to keep permanently
- Cached data you want to reuse between sessions
- Output files to share across multiple sessions
- Configuration or state that should survive session cleanup

{% endif %}

{% if external_mounts.user_ro %}
## User-Specific Read-Only Mounts (`./external/user-ro/`)

These folders are mounted specifically for your user account, read-only:

{% for mount in external_mounts.user_ro %}
- `./external/user-ro/{{ mount.name }}/` {% if mount.description %}- {{ mount.description }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if external_mounts.user_rw %}
## User-Specific Read-Write Mounts (`./external/user-rw/`)

These folders are mounted specifically for your user account, read-write:

{% for mount in external_mounts.user_rw %}
- `./external/user-rw/{{ mount.name }}/` {% if mount.description %}- {{ mount.description }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if dynamic_mounts %}
## Dynamic Mounts

This session has the following user-selected dynamic mounts available at workspace root:

| Alias | Path | Mode | Description |
|-------|------|------|-------------|
{% for mount in dynamic_mounts %}
| {{ mount.alias }} | `./{{ mount.alias }}` | {{ mount.mode }} | {{ mount.description or 'User-requested mount' }} |
{% endfor %}

**Usage:**
- Access files using paths like `./{{ dynamic_mounts[0].alias }}/filename`
- All Ag3ntum tools (mcp__ag3ntum__Read, mcp__ag3ntum__Write, mcp__ag3ntum__Edit, mcp__ag3ntum__Bash, mcp__ag3ntum__Glob, mcp__ag3ntum__Grep) work with dynamic mounts
{% for mount in dynamic_mounts %}
{% if mount.mode == 'ro' %}
- `{{ mount.alias }}` is **read-only** - you cannot modify files in this mount
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}

{% if original_path_mounts %}
## Original-Path Mounts

These paths are accessible at their **original filesystem locations**:

| Path | Mode | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
{% for mount in original_path_mounts %}
| `{{ mount.path }}` | {{ mount.mode }} | {{ mount.description or 'Original-path mount' }} |
{% endfor %}

**Usage:**
- Access files directly at their original paths (e.g., `{{ original_path_mounts[0].path }}/filename`)
- All Ag3ntum tools work with these paths
{% for mount in original_path_mounts %}
{% if mount.mode == 'ro' %}
- `{{ mount.path }}` is **read-only** - you cannot modify files in this path
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}

## Important Notes

1. **Read-only access**: You cannot write to `./external/ro/` or `./external/user-ro/` paths. Attempts will fail with "read-only external mount" error.
2. **Relative paths**: Access mounts using relative paths like `./external/ro/downloads/file.txt`.
3. **File changes**: Changes to writable mounts and `./persistent/` are immediately visible to the host system.

{% endif %}

IMPORTANT: When user provides fully-qualified path to a LOCAL file or folder, check if it's available via `mcp__ag3ntum__LS` tool. 
